253
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:35,660
What happened? Oh, I had a disagreement with my editor.

254
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:38,980
Dad, she made Mom look like a complete...

255
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:41,460
Carol. I've got it on tape, Dad.

256
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:46,560
You decide. No, now, Carol, you just don't understand who adults talk to.

257
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:47,920
Adults sometimes say, yeah.

258
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:50,780
Haven't you seen the new Jack Klugman show?

259
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:55,580
Sure, sure. That must be it.

260
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:59,980
What happened? Oh, no big deal.

261
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:02,200
That's good. You know, the way she's carrying on.

262
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,240
I thought it was the end of the world.

263
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:08,560
No. Hey, you remember Hal Miller, doctor from Long Island General?

264
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:10,260
Well, he came by here today and he offered you...

265
00:15:10,260 --> 00:15:12,000
Oh, Jason. What?

266
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:14,820
I have never been so humiliated in all my life.

267
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:18,640
Honey, what? It is not being yelled at that really bothered me, but are even making

268
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:19,640
the mistake to begin with.

269
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:22,420
What mistake? I used a K instead of an A.

270
00:15:24,020 --> 00:15:26,020
No. In a man's name.

271
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:27,320
Well, that's not so bad.

272
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:29,660
Who will probably sue us because we said he was a felon.

273
00:15:29,660 --> 00:15:31,400
That could be trouble.

274
00:15:32,020 --> 00:15:34,660
But you know what really, really got to me?

275
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:37,780
No. It's what kept going through my head when Susan was yelling at me.

276
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:41,700
What? That instead of working, I could be home doing the laundry.

277
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:44,660
And it sounded good.

278
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:47,600
Oh, you weren't thinking straight.

279
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:51,820
Oh, Jason, it's time I faced a few things, and I need your advice.

280
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:57,960
Okay. Okay? Over this past year, I've had a lot of fears about going back to work.

281
00:15:58,240 --> 00:16:01,580
Mm -hmm. Can I pick up right where I left off 18 years ago?

282
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,460
Can I compete with people half...

283
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:06,160
three -quarters my age?

284
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:11,040
Do I really want a career, or is it the idea of having a career that I love?

285
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:12,940
Am I being fair to the kids?

286
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:14,720
Am I being fair to you?

287
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:17,500
So I did what you always do.

288
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:20,080
I started two lists.

289
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:25,200
Good. One of reasons to keep my job.

290
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:28,320
See, it's blank.

291
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:31,560
And the other reasons to quit.

292
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:35,240
Look at it.

293
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:37,220
Bread, milk, pantyhose?

294
00:16:37,340 --> 00:16:38,840
No, no, no, the other side.

295
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:47,400
Well, this is, uh, quite a list.

296
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,740
So, what do you think?

297
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,820
Are you asking me if I think you should quit?

298
00:16:57,240 --> 00:17:03,020
Yeah. Well, it's interesting that you should ask me this today of all days.

299
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:05,320
Oh, honey, I need your advice.

300
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:07,000
I know you'll be fair and objective.

301
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:11,740
Yes. See, you were the one that advised me to go back to work when in your heart of

302
00:17:11,740 --> 00:17:12,920
hearts you didn't want me to.

303
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:14,660
Well, I did, yes.

304
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:16,380
Yes, and I love you for it.

305
00:17:16,940 --> 00:17:21,620
Thank you. So I know you'll be fair and objective here, too, even if you really

306
00:17:21,620 --> 00:17:25,100
wanted me to quit, because I know staying at home has to be getting to you.

307
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:27,060
Well, I've done...

308
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:27,900
Should I quit?

309
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,820
Oh, that's tough, Maggie.

310
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:32,400
Honey, what do you think?

311
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:41,880
Well, I think that, uh, if you think that you've made a mistake going back to work,

312
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:45,260
then I think, uh, then you should, uh...

313
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:49,420
Do something about it.

314
00:17:54,020 --> 00:17:56,720
Well... I guess that's all there is to say.

315
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:02,020
Mom, I just heard, and I still love you, even if you are a rotten reporter.

316
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:06,180
Good morning! Save it.

317
00:18:06,180 --> 00:18:07,420
It's just me.

318
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:09,100
Then get out of my chair.

319
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:11,340
I was just warming it for you.

320
00:18:12,860 --> 00:18:13,980
Out of my chair, squirt.

321
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:20,340
Where's Mom? She left for work early to clear some things up with her boss.

322
00:18:21,180 --> 00:18:22,260
How do you know?

323
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:26,580
I'm small. People forget I'm around and say all kinds of things.

324
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:31,580
You guys should have told her that you still believe in her and that you're behind

325
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:35,280
her. Hey, Mom doesn't need to hear that from us as long as Dad's around.

326
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:36,460
That's what he's here for.

327
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:37,740
That's why people get married.

328
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:41,660
So that there's at least one person saying you're okay when you know you're just a

329
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:42,720
crummy You can't bag a dog me.

330
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,480
Mike, you're absolutely right.

331
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,980
You guys are gonna have to clean up here and lock the door when you leave.

332
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:52,480
I'm gonna go catch Mom before she makes a mistake.

333
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:57,540
She shouldn't give up because of one little mistake.

334
00:18:57,980 --> 00:18:58,900
She knows that.

335
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,800
I mean, after you were born, she had another kid, didn't she?

336
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:10,880
That's funny. Here.

337
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:15,240
You said yesterday that you wanted a real reporter to do the follow -up to my story.

338
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:16,740
Well, you've got one.

339
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:19,860
Me. You find anything wrong with that, and I'm out of here for good.

340
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:23,500
But if you don't find anything wrong with it, I expect you to use it because it's as

341
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,220
good as anybody can do in this office.

342
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:28,600
You're right. And I don't think it's very fair that you just...

343
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:32,660
What? I said...

344
00:19:32,660 --> 00:19:34,940
You're right. Oh.

345
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:36,260
I'll tell him.

346
00:19:36,260 --> 00:19:37,400
She doesn't know what she's saying.

347
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:38,600
She doesn't mean a word of it.

348
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:40,900
What? Yes, I do.

349
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:41,700
No, you don't.

350
00:19:41,940 --> 00:19:42,960
Yes, I do.

351
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:46,280
I just want you to know that I don't want you to quit.

352
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:48,780
Quit? I am not going to quit.

353
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:50,980
No? No. No.

354
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:54,900
This isn't the Daily Planet?

355
00:19:58,700 --> 00:20:02,000
Excuse me. Lois?

356
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:08,020
Clark? Jimmy? Yes, baby.

357
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:11,980
Jason, what were you thinking?

358
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:14,680
At which embarrassing point?

359
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:16,480
Are you trying to get me fired?

360
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:18,280
No, I came down here to keep you from quitting.

361
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:20,260
Yesterday you told me to quit.

362
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:21,620
Well, that was bad advice.

363
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:22,740
That I relied on.

364
00:20:22,980 --> 00:20:26,420
Well, today I rushed down here to stop you from following it.

365
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,860
Why didn't you follow it?

366
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:31,300
Because it was bad advice.

367
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:34,520
Okay, I admit it.

368
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:39,460
I liked the idea of you coming back and taking over the house, Maggie.

369
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:40,740
I've been feeling trapped.

370
00:20:41,420 --> 00:20:44,800
And you saw Long Island General as a way out?

371
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:47,020
You knew about that?

372
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:52,420
When I was leaving this morning, I happened to find this.

373
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:55,180
Reasons to take the job,

374
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,840
reasons to turn it down.

375
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:00,820
I guess you probably read it, too.

376
00:21:01,440 --> 00:21:03,920
Yep. Both columns.

377
00:21:04,940 --> 00:21:07,460
Jason, why didn't you tell me about the offer?

378
00:21:08,020 --> 00:21:11,920
Well, because I didn't want it to seem like I was telling you to quit so that I

379
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:14,120
could pursue my opportunity,

380
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:16,260
which I was.

381
00:21:18,060 --> 00:21:20,400
You really want to take Hal's offer, don't you?

382
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:25,240
I considered it.

383
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:27,260
And then I made out this list.

384
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:30,540
And, uh, it came out clearly against.

385
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:35,700
Jason, it's nine to one in favor of taking the job.

386
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:39,900
Yes, but the one reason not to,

387
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:43,680
the one called Maggie, that's more important to me than all the rest.

388
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:50,140
You're terrific. Okay, well, it's only fair, you know.

389
00:21:50,140 --> 00:21:54,720
I, uh, I guess it's my turn to stay home with Gilligan and the skipper and the

390
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:57,760
millionaires. We gotta ask Mike.

391
00:21:57,940 --> 00:21:59,560
He's the new philosopher of the family.

392
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:12,780
Oh. Mr. Perlow's feelings of paranoia have been greatly reduced by the realization

393
00:22:12,780 --> 00:22:14,420
of the fact that he is indeed

394
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:16,460
universally disliked.

395
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:18,820
On the bright side...

396
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:20,700
Yeah? In here, Carol.

397
00:22:21,140 --> 00:22:23,380
Huh, honey? How was career day?

398
00:22:23,380 --> 00:22:26,800
Well, see, I realized that most jobs hang by a slender thread.

399
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:30,980
So I decided not to do Mom's job, and I did Emily Sullivan's father's job instead.

400
00:22:31,140 --> 00:22:32,060
What does he do?

401
00:22:32,380 --> 00:22:34,320
He's a clerk at the unemployment office.

402
00:22:35,940 --> 00:22:37,000
Hey, great news, Dad.

403
00:22:37,220 --> 00:22:39,480
I heard it once, I heard it a hundred times today.

404
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:43,620
When I was sick, every teacher mentioned that it was not the same there without me

405
00:22:43,620 --> 00:22:45,720
disrupting class and making stupid comments.

406
00:22:47,780 --> 00:22:48,900
That's great news.

407
00:22:49,360 --> 00:22:50,560
Yeah, well, it is to me.

408
00:22:50,820 --> 00:22:54,180
I mean, the 10th grade may not revolve around me, But they sure know when I'm not

409
00:22:54,180 --> 00:22:56,100
there. Hey, Carol, come on.

410
00:22:56,180 --> 00:22:56,640
Gilligan's on him.

411
00:22:56,640 --> 00:22:57,980
We can't stop him.

412
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:03,200
Thus ends another day in the life of a great psychiatrist.

413
00:23:04,140 --> 00:23:10,920
Not behind the facade of a big city hospital, but right here in the real world.

414
00:23:38,080 --> 00:23:40,880
Thank you.
